From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:13:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] recore: drop the PXE and DHCP boot targets

When nothing bootable is found, distro_bootcmd tries eight
pxelinux.cfg names and then DHCP, and each waits out a PHY
auto-negotiation timeout. On a board that never netboots, that adds
about a minute before the boot failure is reported. Remove the network
boot targets. The dhcp, tftp and pxe commands stay available.

Signed-off-by: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
---
 include/configs/sunxi-common.h | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/configs/sunxi-common.h b/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
index 9cd97f1d..e92447c7 100644
--- a/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
+++ b/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
@@ -222,9 +222,7 @@
 	func(FEL, fel, na) \
 	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_MMC(func) \
 	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_SCSI(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_USB(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_PXE(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_DHCP(func)
+	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_USB(func)
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_OLD_SUNXI_KERNEL_COMPAT
 #define BOOTCMD_SUNXI_COMPAT \
-- 
2.47.3

